==== Wireless Ethernet Dispatch (WED) HW Acceleration ====

These instructions were tested on v24.10. WED is disabled by default, and it may not be completely stable. If you run into issues, try disabling it, and/or removing bridger to see if it resolves your issue.

Edit ''/etc/modules.d/mt7915e'' so that it contains:

<file>mt7915e wed_enable=Y</file>

Then restart the router. Check that WED has been enabled:

<code>
cat /sys/module/mt7915e/parameters/wed_enable
Y
</code>

If you are using the device as a bridged AP, you'll need to [[faq:how_to_install_packages|install]] the [[https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/tree/master/package/network/services/bridger|bridger package]] for it to accelerate traffic streams.

You can check that streams are being accelerated by checking the output of ''cat /sys/kernel/debug/ppe0/bind'', the output should be a list of details on each accelerated stream.
